    "detail": "Pull request #679 changed several parts of ci.yml. It set AGENT_MODEL and AGENT_MODEL_FALLBACK in the workflow env. It installed zizmor and gave `pnpm lint` a GH_TOKEN. It passed HEAD_SHA to needs-e2e.sh. It added a step that takes the bypass secret out of the test results before upload, and it changed the artifact path to `test-results*`. It made usage-limit.sh `start` choose the review's model, and it scrubbed tokens from the transcripts before keeping them. It also added three Neon steps: a reset of the preview's branch when that branch has had a migration the commit lacks, a deletion of production's people, and a `delete-preview` job.\n\nRun 45172033039 on #685 reached every non-Neon change, and each one worked. The `env` block showed AGENT_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5. zizmor 1.33.1 installed, and lint ran with the token. needs-e2e.sh got HEAD_SHA and said there was no apps folder. The redaction step passed with no results to clean, and the upload found no files without failing. The review ran with `--model claude-opus-5-5` read from MODEL. The scrub passed, and the transcript artifact uploaded after it.\n\nThe run skipped every Neon step, because `vars.NEON_PROJECT_ID` is empty in this repository. For the same reason `delete-preview` never ran. Ryan's unchecked assumption has therefore not been tested in a real run. That assumption is that Drizzle's `created_at` equals the journal's `when` in milliseconds, and that its `hash` is the SHA-256 of the migration file's raw text. The first project with Neon and its own migration will be the first test. If the assumption is wrong, every such preview's branch is reset on each push.",
